==Special Moves==
====Hurricane Upper====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=joe_236A,joe_236C,joe_236AC,joe_236ac_6a
|input=236A/C/AC
|input2=qcf+A/C/AC
|description4=
Joe's signature grounded projectile. As with Preecha, the tornadoes linger a bit before dissipating
* A version travels half screen
* C version launches two tornadoes that travel about 70% of the screen
** This version can be braked to launch only one tornado and be safer against jumps
* AC version launches a stationary 3-hit tornado which can be followed up with 6P to launch another 3-hit tornado that travels nearly full screen.
** The follow up can be delayed significantly and can be performed as long as the initial tornado hasn't disappeared.
** If the follow up is performed quickly, the follow up scales the combo as if were a separate EX move and massively reduces damage potential, especially in shorter combos. This may be a bug.

Caution: This special move has a massive flaw in which it is both negative on block AND HIT.Even on counter hit, Joe is only +2 with alot of pushback. Despite being a safe and effective block string ender, opponents who understand this flaw can make Joe think twice before using this move to end block strings. But for the most part,this move is Joe's safest block string ender and should be used as needed.
}}

====Slash Kick====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Slash Kick
|moveId=joe_236b,joe_236d,joe_236bd
|input=236B/D/BD
|input2=qcf+B/D/BD
|description3=
A leaping forward kick, kind of like Terry's Burning Knuckle.
* All versions can be braked before they hit. This can be useful for baiting reversals or approaching for throws.
* B version can technically be safe on block when spaced but very difficult in practice. Joe will more often than not be point blank and -5 or worse at most ranges this move is attempted from.

Avoid using the D and REV version for the most part as they doesn't serve much purpose in Joe's kit and gameplan. The REV version is quite situational, it should only be used when Joe is in SPG to make it safe, and even then its not that worth going for.
}}

====Tiger Kick====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Tiger Kick
|moveId=joe_623b,joe_623d,joe_623bd
|input=623B/D/BD
|input2=dp+B/D/BD
|description3=
A rising knee strike. BD version has Joe charge forward slightly with a tackle before doing the Tiger Kick.
* Good horizontal range for a DP and always hits as long as far A hits, which many other characters cannot do with their DPs.
* At longer ranges, the D version's brakeable frames end before it can hit. This happens if 3 lights are used before the DP or from a close D > far A link.
