==Super Special Moves==
====Screw Upper====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Screw Upper
|moveId=joe_236236A,joe_236236C
|input=236236A/C
|input2=qcfqcf+A/C
|description2=
Joe does an uppercut with his outside fist, launching his opponent. He then uses his main arm to launch a massive tornado.Extremely combo-friendly and easy to end combos with.
* This is Joe's reversal super and is fully invincible and faster than his other super.
* Joe will be at close D range and +17 on a ground hit and +19 on a juggle after 2 dashes after the A version of this move.

The C version of this super has a very interesting property that is hard to see at first. The 2nd hit actually launches a massive fullscreen tornado that is a true projectile. Using this when the opponent is in overheat and full screen can be a very cheeky way to get a chip kill or chip damage.
}}

====Screw Elbow====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|name=Screw Elbow
|moveId=joe_236236B,joe_236236D,joe_236236d_d
|input=236236B/D
|input2=qcfqcf+B/D
|description3=
Joe rears his arms back and spins it, gathering gales into his fist. He then unleashes it forwards in a torrent that blasts the opponent away fullscreen.This is Joe's best combo ender but is much less combo friendly as a trade off. This super also has much worse okizeme than screw upper
* The opponent ends up nearly at fullscreen distance and Joe gets no oki off of this.
** However, this may be work to his advantage because he can transition to his strong zoning game.
* The D version of this move sets wallbounces like a AA counter REV blow and sets up a juggle.
** Joe can also perform a free follow-up with D. Simply holding down D will also cause this follow-up to occur.
** Charging the follow-up prevents the opponent from leaving the corner from the wallbounce.
}}

